# Re-apply the stored CPU governor mode whenever the charger is plugged or
# unplugged, so "auto" (the default) keeps tracking AC status even when
# nothing else is watching -- penrose not running, or between an `M-q`
# rebuild and its restart. See ~/env/scripts/cpu-governor-apply.sh.
#
# This runs as root already, so unlike 99-batify.rules's RUN+= entries there
# is no session-bus dance needed -- but power-profiles-daemon's own polkit
# policy only authorizes an *active* session, which a udev worker has none
# of, hence ~/env/polkit-rules/60-cpu-governor.rules.

SUBSYSTEM=="power_supply", KERNEL=="AC", ACTION=="change", \
RUN+="/home/mgsloan/env/scripts/cpu-governor-apply.sh"
